# CO-ARCH-002 — Enterprise Data Protection & Non-Destructive Development

Status: **FROZEN** · Authority: Product Owner · Priority: **CRITICAL**  
Full text: `docs/governance/CO-ARCH-002-ENTERPRISE-DATA-PROTECTION.md`

## Principle

Enterprise Data is SSOT. Default: **READ · EXTEND · NEVER DESTROY.**

Under no circumstances may implementation, enhancement, refactoring, optimisation, or feature work **modify, delete, reset, reseed, recreate, truncate, corrupt**, or otherwise affect existing enterprise data unless the Product Owner **explicitly** authorises it.

## Allowed (additive)

- New UI, screens, modules, services, registries  
- Extend APIs  
- Backward-compatible schema additions  
- UX / performance improvements  

## Forbidden without Product Owner authorisation

- Delete / mutate production business records  
- Reset IDs · reseed · truncate · rename enterprise tables  
- Remove enterprise relationships or break existing APIs  
- Destructive migrations  
- Remove working business logic when extension suffices  
- Replace working implementations when extension is sufficient  

## Live data

Never alter live enterprise data during feature development.  
Test needs → isolated demo / local mock / fixtures only.

## When in doubt

**STOP.** Request Product Owner approval before any change that might touch existing data.

## Scope

Catalyst One · Catalyst Connect · COMPASS · CHANAKYA · every registry · every future sprint.  
Supersedes implementation convenience.
